		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=5022&amp;p=36815#p36815"><![CDATA[
<blockquote class="uncited"><div><blockquote class="uncited"><div><blockquote class="uncited"><div><br><br>for the TYT MD-UV390 Plus with GPS and 10W you must use the file: <strong class="text-strong">OpenMDUV380_10W_PLUS.zip</strong></div></blockquote>Dispongo del cable correcto, el problema es que con el OpenMDUV380_10W_PLUS.zip se me queda la pantalla en negro sin iluminacion, con el firmware normal de 380 si se ilumina y funciona bien.<br>Desconozco si es normal y si existe algúna solución en mi caso.<br><br>En la etiqueta del aparato puede leerse:<br>MD-UV390<br>Output 10W<br>Con pegatina roja redonda arriba a la derecha con las letras PLUS.<hr style="height:10px;border:0;box-shadow:0 10px 10px -10px #8c8b8b inset">I have the correct cable, but the problem is that with the OpenMDUV380_10W_PLUS.zip, the screen goes black with no light.<br>With the regular 380 normal firmware it lights up and works fine.<br>I don't know if this is normal or if there's a solution for my case.<br><br>The device's label reads:<br>MD-UV390<br>10W Output<br>With a round red sticker in the top right corner with the letters PLUS.</div></blockquote>Hi!<br> I got the same radio today. Mine also has the "PLUS" sticker and says "10W", so I assumed it was the 10W PLUS version.<br><br> But, just like you found, when I tried the "380 10w plus" firmware, I encountered the same screen problems and couldn't transmit to my Hotspot either.<br><br>Working great with the 380uv normal version!<br>Thanks!</div></blockquote>"<br>// PA_SEL_SW and LCB_BKLIGHT pins are swapped on the MD-UV390Plus 10W radios<br>#if defined(PLATFORM_VARIANT_UV380_PLUS_10W)<br>#undef PA_SEL_SW_Pin<br>#undef PA_SEL_SW_GPIO_Port<br>#undef LCD_BKLIGHT_Pin<br>#undef LCD_BKLIGHT_GPIO_Port<br>"<br>UV-390 PLUS has different hardware versions, that is, the backlight control and PA selection I/O are interchanged, and it can be solved by modifying the corresponding definition of /Core/Inc/main.h and recompiling it<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=6826">BA7IQE</a> — Fri Apr 18, 2025 4:59 am</p><hr />
]]></content>
